    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "You will carry out a geometry optimisation on a bad guess for H$_2$O\n",
    "with an unrealistic H-O-H angle of 90$^\\circ$ and a O-H distance of 1.5Å. During the optimisation,\n",
    "Psi4 will move the positions of the atoms in the molecule, moving downhill on the potential energy surface, until it finds a minimum. \n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "editable": true,
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": ""
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "source": [
    "First, we define our suboptimal geometry. Again, we use a UHF reference. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {
    "editable": true,
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": ""
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "r = 1.5\n",
    "angle = 90\n",
    "\n",
    "# Water Z-Matrix\n",
    "h2o_suboptimal = psi4.geometry(f\"\"\"\n",
    "O1\n",
    "H2 1 {r}\n",
    "H3 1 {r} 2 {angle}\n",
    "\"\"\")\n",
    "\n",
    "h2o_suboptimal_start = h2o_suboptimal.clone() # we store here the starting geometry for comparison"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {
    "editable": true,
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": ""
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# setting the options to write out the xyz files of the optimization\n",
    "psi4.set_options({'reference':'uhf'})\n",
    "psi4.core.set_output_file(f'h2o-opt.log', False)\n",
    "\n",
    "psi4.set_options({'print_trajectory_xyz_file':True})"
   ]
  },
